// Package models holds this application's documents.
//
// A document is a plain struct with bson tags. There is no ORM: the framework's
// mongo package gives a typed Collection over the driver, and nothing here
// pretends a document is a row.
//
// Each model declares the indexes it needs from init, so importing this package
// is enough for `ry migrate` to find them — which is exactly what app/app.go
// does. That is the whole of what replaces migrations: a document store has no
// schema to migrate, and indexes are the part that genuinely has to be created
// before anything relies on them.
//
// Create one with:
//
//	ry make:model Post
package models
